speaking on behalf of the applicant, Jose Luis Gomez-Salcedo, clarified, pursuant to discussion at
Finance Committee, that this is a new applicant and any prior business financial obligations
involving taxes should be the responsibility of the previous licensee, and requested approval of the
application.  Mr. Spiker moved to approve, seconded by Mr. Collins.  Brief comment in support of
the application was made.  Motion carried.  Voting “yes” – all members of the governing body
present.
OTHER CITY BUSINESS:
John Fafoutakis commented on freedoms enjoyed by Americans, recent newspaper article
concerning City revenue shortfall projections and the need to prioritize expenditures, and expressed
concern with certain items for the meeting being placed on the Consent Agenda, not open to
discussion.  Mayor Kaysen advised the Consent Agenda items referenced were items involving
referrals to Finance Committee where public discussion will be available.
Clarification was made that any member of the public may contact a City Council member
to request an item(s), pursuant to Consent Agenda rules, be removed from the Consent Agenda.
There being no further business to come before the governing body, the meeting was
officially adjourned at 9:28 p.m.
Submitted by,
Carol Intlekofer, MMC
City Clerk
